{"project_name":"codemonkey","programming_languages":["Python"],"summary":"codemonkey is a scriptable, headless coding-agent CLI written in Python 3.11 (uv, Typer, Rich, httpx, with no LLM SDKs) that runs non-interactively against OpenAI-style and Anthropic-style endpoints — including a local llama.cpp server — so it can be driven by other agents and CI pipelines. It provides an interactive REPL plus commands like `exec` (one-shot runs with JSONL event streams, session resume, and structured output via JSON schema), `review`, `sessions`, `journal`, `undo`, and `eval`, backed by a 13-tool agent toolset (shell, file read/write/edit, search, glob, planning, web fetch, repo mapping, memory, and isolated delegation) governed by rule-based permissions and approval policies. Reliability features include per-write checkpoints with undo, post-mutation verify gates, an execution journal with failure taxonomy, idempotent mutating tools, auto-compaction strategies, and pluggable strategy interfaces for compaction, memory, and session state configured via YAML."}[usage] prompt=6764 completion=499
